// 2026-11-01: deletion-propagation fix (PR #21).
{"id": "CL-R6-deletion", "version": 1, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "When code is deleted, only claims and evidence that explicitly depend_on it become unjustified; other records linked to it (an evaluation via depends_on, anything via implemented_by) become needs_review, and transitive propagation through claims is unchanged", "rationale": "WP0 self-reconciliation found deletion over-propagating: every record pointing at deleted code was marked unjustified, though a deletion does not falsify an evaluation or a requirement", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R6@1"}]}
{"id": "EV-R6-deletion-tests", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "method": "PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest tests.test_code_impact (two violating cases fail without the fix; two decoys pass with and without it; full suite 111 OK on 2026-11-01)", "limits": "fixtures only; no real deletion in a governed repo observed yet", "text": "tests/test_code_impact.py: an evaluation that depends_on deleted code and a claim linked by implemented_by become needs_review; evidence with depends_on stays unjustified; transitive propagation unchanged", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R6-deletion@1"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.impact.impact"}]}
// 2026-11-01 dogfood: WP-S and WP1A requirements with source anchors; projections of the canonical round-2 decisions (relay-kit-private, DEC-018).
{"id": "AEC-R9", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-scope", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "A record can point at the source passage it came from; check reports each anchor as verified, missing, mismatch, locator_invalid or unavailable without judging support; source show reads anchored passages and source search finds what no record indexed, labelled fallback (spec 004, WP-S)", "rationale": "What a summary drops, a later agent can't recover from the summary (representation-001). Zach authorized WP-S in Claude chat 2026-10-30 13:07 CT. The authorization is anchored where it was recorded (the spec status line and handoff HO-20261030-001), not in a chat capture.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-R2@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.record_findings"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.render_show"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.render_search"}], "anchors": [{"path": "specs/004-source-anchors/spec.md", "sha256": "14efb890a481814d1a214ab0ace08248ffc715d10e86084b49fdfb15f9482124", "locator": "q:Five capabilities, kept separate", "for": "text"}, {"path": "specs/004-source-anchors/spec.md", "sha256": "14efb890a481814d1a214ab0ace08248ffc715d10e86084b49fdfb15f9482124", "locator": "q:I'm giving the OK to go ahead.", "for": "rationale"}, {"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "handoffs/HO-20261030-001.md", "sha256": "39a285a8f9b9b42e0db53ab90ea2b0b4258f32a8ec82da3663a53e5a90f3d7b2", "locator": "q:WP-S looks good, and I agree with the recommendations from Kate", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "CL-R9-states", "version": 1, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "subject": "aec-scope", "text": "Each spec-004 fixture yields exactly its expected anchor state, the valid-artifact decoy yields no finding, and anchor output never says supports, verifies or authorizes", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R9@1"}]}
{"id": "EV-R9-tests", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "method": "PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest tests.test_sources (25 tests, OK, 2026-11-01 on main@4decef6)", "limits": "conformance to the spec's fixtures only; says nothing about whether anchors help agents recover facts (that is representation-002)", "text": "tests/test_sources.py passes: all five states, the decoy, bounded show/search output, byte-identical reruns and the banned-wording check", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R9-states@1"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.record_findings"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.render_show"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.aec.sources.render_search"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R10", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-scope", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "A snapshot names exactly what it describes (commit, or dirty working tree, and the extraction method), and two snapshots are compared only when their methods match, against the merge base for a PR (spec 005, WP1A). Not yet implemented; three clarifications await Zach", "rationale": "Zach approved the WP1A package in Claude chat 2026-10-30 20:29 CT; anchored to the spec status line that records it.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-R2@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R5@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "specs/005-commit-snapshots/spec.md", "sha256": "b9f58cdfcb6bd2831e508580d68b74c2166a2c616e452e5600a1786a16e417af", "locator": "q:a snapshot names exactly what it describes", "for": "text"}, {"path": "specs/005-commit-snapshots/spec.md", "sha256": "b9f58cdfcb6bd2831e508580d68b74c2166a2c616e452e5600a1786a16e417af", "locator": "q:I approve WP1A.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DEC-016", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-016", "text": "AEC is reframed as a foundation of four guarantees (recover sources; establish authority; check applicability; verify claims) plus an experimental augmentation layer for better agent judgment; amend docs/architecture.md as direction.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-016\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-017", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-017", "text": "Spec three safeguards as one small work package after WP1A: recoverable provenance for consequential authorizations; artifact integrity checked by tools, not reported by models; premise checks before consequential execution.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-017\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-018", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-018", "text": "Ownership boundary: relay-kit owns coordination mechanics (handoffs, delivery, versions, IDs, thread index); AEC owns development semantics (purpose, obligation, evidence, premises); one canonical decision record, hosted in relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl, which AEC references rather than duplicates.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-018\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-019", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-019", "text": "Drift/run principle: information crosses freely; authority never crosses implicitly. Drift threads are round-scoped. Drift includes pilots and feasibility tests (owner addition, 18:11 CT).", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-019\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-020", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-020", "text": "Planning: try for a month a decision queue kept by agents, a candidate-vs-committed distinction, and event-triggered checkpoints instead of Jira, sprints or PI planning.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-020\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-021", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-021", "text": "Queue experiments in ephemeral contexts: the ontology audit (four cases) first, then a minimal-vs-full AEC scenario.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-021\"", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DEC-022", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "subject": "aec-scope", "origin": "projection", "canonical": "relay-kit-private governance/decisions.jsonl DEC-022", "text": "Leave open whether AEC/EACH is one product or a family; for each new component ask whether its benefit depends on integration.", "rationale": "Owner decision: \"Yes, pretty good counts as approval.\" (18:12 CT), answering claude:aec on its reading of \"I read the decisions \u2026 Those are all pretty good.\" (18:11 CT)", "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "4d7340ed49fdecb5f1e4e8e39dc4072392a6d45547b2ff1fb891d2585eaf6090", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-022\"", "for": "text"}]}
